  "theory": {
        "intro": "A cubic $ax^{3}+bx^{2}+cx+d=0$ with roots $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$ gives three combinations built from its coefficients: the sum, the sum of pairs, and the product. Each comes from a coefficient ratio, with no need to solve.",
        "facts": [
          "The signs alternate: $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=-\\dfrac{b}{a}$, $\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma=\\dfrac{c}{a}$, and $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-\\dfrac{d}{a}$.",
          "A missing term has coefficient $0$: in $x^{3}-6x+1=0$, $b=0$ so $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=0$.",
          "When $a \\neq 1$, divide each of $b$, $c$ and $d$ by the leading coefficient $a$.",
          "A monic cubic with roots $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$ is $x^{3}-(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)x^{2}+(\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma)x-\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=0$.",
          "The reciprocal sum is $\\dfrac{1}{\\alpha}+\\dfrac{1}{\\beta}+\\dfrac{1}{\\gamma}=\\dfrac{\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma}=-\\dfrac{c}{d}$."
        ],
        "steps": [
          "Identify coefficients $a, b, c, d$ from standard cubic form $ax^{3}+bx^{2}+cx+d=0$.",
          "Evaluate the single sum $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=-\\dfrac{b}{a}$.",
          "Evaluate the pair sum $\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma=\\dfrac{c}{a}$.",
          "Evaluate the triple product $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-\\dfrac{d}{a}$."
        ]
      },
